================================================================================
DATA AND CONTENT RETRIEVED AT RUNTIME
================================================================================

This application displays content fetched from external services. That content
is not covered by this project's licence and remains subject to the licences and
terms of its sources:

Museum of New Zealand Te Papa Tongarewa — Collections API
  Collection records and images are © Museum of New Zealand Te Papa Tongarewa,
  provided via the Te Papa Collections API and subject to its terms of use.
  Record metadata is licensed CC BY 4.0; images carry their own individual
  licences and rights statements (shown in the app) — check before reuse.
  Te Papa's place and subject metadata draws on external authorities such as the
  Getty Thesaurus of Geographic Names (TGN) and Art & Architecture Thesaurus
  (AAT), which the app surfaces only as reference codes.
  https://www.tepapa.govt.nz/api-terms-of-use

Wikipedia (Wikimedia Foundation)
  Person and place detail panels show a preview (summary text and a thumbnail)
  fetched from the Wikipedia REST API, with a link back to the source article.
  Wikipedia article text is available under the Creative Commons
  Attribution-ShareAlike Licence (CC BY-SA); see the linked article for authors
  and licence. Preview thumbnails are served from Wikimedia Commons and carry
  their own individual licences.
  https://en.wikipedia.org/  •  https://www.wikimedia.org/

Wikidata (Wikimedia Foundation)
  People and organisations are matched to their Wikipedia article via their
  Wikidata identifier. Wikidata is released into the public domain under
  CC0 1.0 Universal.
  https://www.wikidata.org/

OpenStreetMap
  Place records with coordinates link out to a map on openstreetmap.org. Map
  data is © OpenStreetMap contributors, available under the Open Database
  Licence (ODbL).
  https://www.openstreetmap.org/copyright

